      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-243027",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/5c/5c2a57a7a1b727d790343efacd8dd95e226136a358625d4852544e534adae968.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AH^(\u2015)$ bisects angle $\u2220BAC$ and $\u2220ABH\u2245\u2220ACH$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The segments $HB^(\u2015)$ and $HC^(\u2015)$ are congruent.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220ABH\u2245\u2220ACH$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\u2220BAH\u2245\u2220CAH$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $AH^(\u2015)\u2245AH^(\u2015)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\u25b3AHB\u2245\u25b3AHC$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $HB^(\u2015)\u2245HC^(\u2015)$ | {{field-5}} |"
    }
  ],
